{"resourceIdentifier":"2352","resourceName":"Shizaiqian MSW landfill site LFG recovery to power project","description":"Shizaiqian MSW landfill site LFG recovery to power project (hereafter referred to as the project) is located at Shizaiqian MSW landfill site(hereafter referred to as the Shizaiqian landfill site)， in Quanzhou City, Fujian Province, P.R. China. The project is constructed and operated by Quanzhou BCCY New Energy CO.,Ltd. (hereafter referred to as the project owner)\r\nShizaiqian landfill site started collecting and handling waste in 2011.\r\nThe project has a total designed capacity 5MW(5*1MW) and combusts the LFG,which contains nearly 50% of methane,to generate electricity and export it  to the Eastern China Power Grid(ECPG). VCUs will be claimed from the methane destroyed and the grid electricity displaced.The estimated average GHG emission reductions of the project  is 68,668 tCO2e and the total GHG emission reductions and removals are 686,684 tCO2e during the fixed 10 years crediting period.\r\nScenario existing prior to the implementation of the project (the same as baseline scenario):\r\n LFG from Shizaiqian landfill site is emitted to the atmosphere directly.\r\nEquivalent electricity generated by the project is supplied by the Eastern China Power Grid        \r\n(ECPG), which is dominated by fossil fuel based power plants.","location":{"latitude":24.965478,"longitude":118.629433},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-04-10","endExclusive":"2021-05-11","endInclusive":"2021-05-10"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2352"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Fujian Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Quanzhou BCCY New Energy CO., Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"Henan Province, China"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","val